# tests/mmap — MIT #11 mmap + MIT #14 megapages (week 8)

Stub created week 2 (design gate). Syscall semantics in docs/design.md §2.3.

## Planned tests

- `mm-shared`: two procs map the same file MAP_SHARED; counter increments through the
  mapping are visible to both; `msync` + remount-read shows persisted value.
- `mm-private`: MAP_PRIVATE write changes only the mapper's view; file contents and
  other procs see original bytes.
- `mm-msync`: dirty a page, msync, power-cut-style reboot (QEMU relaunch), file holds
  flushed bytes (commit survived via log).
- `mm-megapage`: 2 MB-aligned anon region maps as megapage (debug counter proves
  L1-leaf PTE in use); fault-latency measured 4K vs 2M; partial munmap demotes
  correctly (counter drops, region still functional).
- `mm-faultlat`: bench harness for §"Measure" line of week 8: cycles/fault 4K vs 2M,
  mmap read vs `read()` loop on the same file.

## Pass criteria

shared/private/msync round-trips pass; megapage counter shows promotion then demotion
with no stale-TLB crashes; latency numbers recorded in bench/baseline.txt.
